  "scope_statement": "The five waveform loss terms in scripts/31_surrogate_encoder.py are computed over all 12 displayed leads whenever cfg has no recon_channels key; d1s_r3_s42.yaml has no such key, so recon_rows=None and the four derived leads ARE inside the reconstruction loss. The derivation convention therefore changes the training objective and the fitted parameters. The invariance reported here is only that, for a FIXED trained decoder evaluated at analysis time, the FIM restricted to the 8 non-derived leads is bitwise identical under the two conventions (the derived rows are simply not in the row set). Over all 12 displayed leads the FIM is NOT invariant. No claim is made that a model retrained under the other convention would have the same FIM.",
